-- a canvas already hears a pointer --
  the press arrived: true
  in the canvas's own points: true
  and the platform carried it: true
-- the same point, as the shader sees it --
  a quarter across and three tenths down: true
  a canvas with no size says so: true
-- taking the keyboard is asked for, not assumed --
  one that has not asked is refused: true
  one that asked says so: true
  then it takes the keyboard: true
  and knows it has it: true
  turning it off puts it back: true
-- and only a canvas may be told --
  a button is refused: true
-- what a canvas calls itself --
  by default, what its kind says: true
  told it is a button, it says button: true
  told it is an image, it says image: true
  and put back, its kind answers again: true
  a button may not claim one: true
-- and what it is called --
  a canvas can be named: true
  and so can a button: true
  an unnamed button is announced by its title: true
  an unnamed canvas is announced by nothing: true
